<title>GERMANY: Continental details 1996 results by units.</title>
<headline>Continental details 1996 results by units.</headline>
<dateline>HANOVER, Germany 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German tyre manufacturer Continental AG gave the following breakdown of its results by operating units in its 1996 annual report.</p>
<p>(Results in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>Passenger Tyre Group:</p>
<p>    Sales				   4,228  vs  4,079</p>
<p>    EBIT earnings			   334  vs    251</p>
<p>    Capital spending			265  vs    268</p>
<p>    Depreciation			    258  vs    237</p>
<p>    Total assets			  3,155  vs  3,180</p>
<p>    Workforce			    19,866  vs 21,584</p>
<p>Commercial Vehicle Tyre Group:</p>
<p>    Sales				   1,073  vs 1,170</p>
<p>    EBIT earnings loss		     23  vs     5 profit</p>
<p>    Capital spending			 64  vs    66</p>
<p>    Depreciation			     65  vs    62</p>
<p>    Total assets			    899  vs   921</p>
<p>    Workforce			     4,227  vs 4,735</p>
<p>Continental General Tyre Group:</p>
<p>    Sales				   2,058  vs 2,062</p>
<p>    EBIT earnings			    82  vs    56</p>
<p>    Capital spending			 87  vs   120</p>
<p>    Depreciation			    145  vs   121</p>
<p>    Total assets			  1,628  vs 1,565</p>
<p>    Workforce			     6,248  vs 6,981</p>
<p>ContiTech Group:</p>
<p>    Sales				   2,968  vs  2,795</p>
<p>    EBIT earnings			   177  vs    121</p>
<p>    Capital spending			149  vs    153</p>
<p>    Depreciation			    133  vs    131</p>
<p>    Total assets			  1,593  vs  1,576</p>
<p>    Workforce			    14,199  vs 14,396</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
